// Character bakes of the art pass (docs/ROADMAP.md, "Art pass
// (pre-stream)"), run by `just art-bake` (`inspect_gltf bake`, see
// tools/inspect_gltf/src/bake.rs). Each row poses a rigged KayKit
// Adventurers character from the download cache (`just fetch-assets`; its
// sources.tsv rows have dest `-`) at one moment of a clip, keeps the named
// nodes, and writes a static GLB under assets/ whose asset.extras record the
// ATTRIBUTION.md Modifications text.
//
// Row fields:
//   out          output path under assets/; its file stem is the kind
//                (`just art-bake --only shieldbearer`)
//   src          source file name in the cache (Knight.glb, Rogue.glb, ...)
//   texture      optional: a texture file in the cache to embed instead of
//                the source's own image
//   keep         node-name globs (`*` matches any run); a node is kept when
//                a glob matches its own name
//   pose         (clip: "Idle", at_ms: 0); STEP and LINEAR keys, CUBICSPLINE
//                fails
//   max_texture  largest side; a larger texture is halved until it fits, only
//                when every face keeps its colour
//   yaw_deg      optional, default 90: turns glTF's +Z front to +X
//
// Measured in slice 2 (`inspect_gltf inspect`): every character is a 41-joint
// rig at rest in a T-pose (arm-span ratio 1.09 on the Knight), its clips are
// LINEAR (76 on the Knight, including "Idle"), and its texture is a 1024x1024
// PNG embedded in the .glb. Body plus kept items are 4,005 to 5,325
// triangles. The rows are written in slice 4, e.g.
//   (out: "models/kaykit_adventurers/shieldbearer.glb", src: "Knight.glb",
//    keep: ["Knight_*", "Rectangle_Shield", "1H_Sword"],
//    pose: (clip: "Idle", at_ms: 0), max_texture: 256),
(
  models: [],
)
